# UI Component Workflow

## Project structure

```
src/ui/
├── primitives/      ← LOCAL components (copied from reactnativereusables + adapted)
│   ├── checkbox.tsx ← fetched from rnr, NativeWind removed, Unistyles applied
│   └── index.ts
├── components/      ← app-level compositions built on top of primitives
│   ├── FormField/
│   │   └── index.tsx
│   └── index.ts
└── theme/           ← colors, spacing, fonts, breakpoints (read-only reference)
```

---

## STEP 1 — Before writing any code, follow this checklist

### A. Check local primitives first

1. Read `src/ui/primitives/` — if the component already exists, use it from there.
   - Import as: `@/ui/primitives/<name>`
   - Never reach back to `@rn-primitives/*` from `src/ui/components/`

2. If the component does NOT exist locally:
   - Fetch the source from the reactnativereusables GitHub registry:
     ```
     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrzachnugent/react-native-reusables/main/packages/registry/src/new-york/components/ui/<name>.tsx
     ```
   - Adapt it using the NativeWind → Unistyles conversion rules below
   - Place the adapted file in `src/ui/primitives/<name>.tsx`
   - Install only the minimum required packages (usually just `@rn-primitives/<name>`)

3. If the component doesn't exist on reactnativereusables either, build it with plain RN primitives (`Pressable`, `View`, `Text`).

### B. When design screens are provided

Study every image in detail before asking anything. Then ask only about what is genuinely unclear:

- All interactive states: default, pressed, focused, disabled, loading, error, success
- Spacing or dimensions that differ from theme tokens (`src/ui/theme/metrics.ts`)
- Colors: match to tokens in `src/ui/theme/colors.ts`; ask if a color is not in the theme
- Typography: match font size/weight to `src/ui/theme/fonts.ts`
- Corner radius, shadow, border width
- Animation behavior (does it animate? what kind?)
- Dark mode variant: is one provided?

**Do NOT write any code until all states and ambiguities are resolved by the user.**

### C. Standard clarifying questions (ask when not obvious)

- Is there a loading / skeleton state?
- Are there size variants (sm / md / lg)?
- Are there style variants (primary / secondary / destructive / ghost)?
- Does it appear in a list (performance considerations)?
- Should it forward a `ref`?

